From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000234 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 13:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: repair state-owner initialization boundary

The enabled owner-profile compile shows that an earlier zero-context hunk
placed the state-owner mutex initializer inside the snapshot validation branch
instead of the handoff probe, and left a duplicate handoff error tail at
end-of-file after the helper was repaired. Move the initializer to the probe
setup and remove only the duplicate tail. No hardware operation or runtime
policy is changed.

This is an experiment-only build-repair patch and is not submission-ready.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-handoff.c | 4 ----
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-handoff.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-handoff.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-handoff.c
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-handoff.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-handoff.c
@@ -1680,1 +1680,0 @@
-	mutex_init(&handoff->state_owner_lock);
@@ -2964,3 +2964,0 @@
-	return ERR_PTR(ret);
-}
-EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mt6797_dvfsp_handoff_get);
@@ -2981,5 +2981,6 @@ static int mt6797_dvfsp_handoff_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	handoff->initial_gate = MT6797_DVFSP_GATE_UNKNOWN;
 	handoff->reason = "resources-not-ready";
 	mutex_init(&handoff->lock);
+	mutex_init(&handoff->state_owner_lock);
 	mutex_init(&handoff->transfer_lock);
 	mutex_init(&handoff->fw_owner_lock);
-- 
2.43.0
